    <p class="eyebrow">The questions</p>
    <p>The books begin from a single concern: what a culture loses when its center empties, and what it takes to form a life — and a civilization — back toward something that holds. They ask what is coming apart in the age of AI, and whether the change we are inside of is going somewhere or merely away.</p>

    <p class="eyebrow">The stance</p>
    <p>The work is written as a declared witness — not a neutral survey, and not a concealed argument. Every opposing ground is given its full strength; the loss is diagnosed as ours, not theirs. The reader is asked for nothing but the willingness to examine: ideas are good or bad on their own merits, and this work follows the evidence wherever honest inquiry leads.</p>

    <p class="eyebrow">The writer</p>
